Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Sun Sep 20 07:32:29 2026 +0000

    A mutable variable imported through an api assigns and reads back when compiled

    Mutability was lost twice on the way across the api boundary and both sites
    are repaired: the checker asked the importing component's type environment
    whether an api-qualified name was mutable, so it refused every such assignment
    with "Cannot assign to immutable variable" before codegen was reached; and
    CodeGen.forVarRef's fresh-import path built a plain StaticBinding with the
    value's descriptor while a mutable variable's singleton field holds R1's
    MutableFValue cell, so the run died with NoSuchFieldError. The class-name half
    of ledger row 320 is deliberately not repaired and is reclassified: it is the
    repository's missing "which component exports this api" step, it hits exported
    functions identically, and it never reaches codegen through fortress link or
    through walk -- it lands as a gated expected failure instead.

    Gated by compiler_tests/ExportVarRungX.test, with the refusal the widened
    check must not lose gated beside it by XXXExportVarRungXFrozen.test and the
    deferred half by XXXExportVarRungXLinked.test. Two new ledger rows, 343 and
    344, both from the rung's skeptic: the row the rung first wrote asserted that
    the interpreter cannot see an api-exported mutable variable at all, which the
    skeptic's name-isolation measurement refuted, and it is not opened.

    historical: ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/compiler/codegen/CodeGen.java,
    ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/scala_src/typechecker/STypeChecker.scala,
    ProjectFortress/src/com/sun/fortress/scala_src/typechecker/impls/Operators.scala

    Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
